      "problem": "Which of the following is congruent to $0$ modulo $7?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall that \n\n$$\na≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a=kn,\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in Z.$ In other words, when $a$ is divided by $n,$ there is no remainder. This means that any integer multiple of $7$ is congruent to $0$ modulo $7.$\n\nTherefore, since $7\\,|\\,35,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n35≡5\\cdot 7≡5\\cdot 0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\nNone of the other options are multiples of $7.$",
